  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow` applies. The requirement says a skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps.\n\nThe first heading section after the title is `section[Bootstrap requirements]/section[Workflow]`. Every other `##` section follows it: Inventories, Proposing requirements, Tagging, Report and Gotchas. The Workflow section is a numbered list of steps 1 to 9, with sub-steps under step 7. These are ordered steps.\n\nTwo short paragraphs sit under the `#` title before `## Workflow`. They have no heading of their own, so they are preamble to the title section and not a separate section. The other skills I looked at (`habeas-evidence`, `habeas-refactor` and `habeas-requirements`) also put a short preamble before `## Workflow`.\n\nI read the requirement as constraining sections. If it were read to forbid any prose before the workflow, this file would break it. I don't think the wording supports that reading equally well, because it says \"before any other section\".",
